 "notes": [
  "'ms120' keeps its address 10.180.16.15 on 'mx-vlan20' as an addressed leg: a native switch has no SVI in v1, so it is not deployed (NSW-080, S2)",
  "the tables' STP bridge priorities and port costs have no field on a native switch and are not carried",
  "'mx-sw' <-> 'ms120' port 'sfp26' is the redundant link STP blocked (higher cost): written `state: blocked`; with `stp: rstp` on both switches it would fail over instead (but RSTP, not the table's cost, then picks the blocked port)",
  "8 VM leg(s) would auto-attach to another switch (or tie between carriers, NSW-040): wired by explicit access links to the switch the table puts them on",
  "tap/default.yaml: the binding on 'vlan20' now names 'mx-vlan20': on a native switch a segment binding mirrors every VM port on the VLAN, across its switches (D8)",
  "tap/default.yaml: the binding on 'vlan1' now names 'mx-vlan1': on a native switch a segment binding mirrors every VM port on the VLAN, across its switches (D8)",
  "tap/fanout-suricata.yaml: the binding on 'vlan20' now names 'mx-vlan20': on a native switch a segment binding mirrors every VM port on the VLAN, across its switches (D8)",
  "tap/fanout-suricata.yaml: the binding on 'vlan1' now names 'mx-vlan1': on a native switch a segment binding mirrors every VM port on the VLAN, across its switches (D8)",
  "tap/gate90.yaml: the binding on 'vlan20' now names 'mx-vlan20': on a native switch a segment binding mirrors every VM port on the VLAN, across its switches (D8)",
  "tap/gate90.yaml: the binding on 'vlan1' now names 'mx-vlan1': on a native switch a segment binding mirrors every VM port on the VLAN, across its switches (D8)",
  "tap/uplink-span.yaml: ['sfp25'] joins ['ms120', 'mx-sw']; the SPAN session is put on 'ms120' (the deeper one -- a veth link mirrors the same frames at either end)",
  "the planner assigns the VLAN tags (from 2 upward): a twin config has no field for the real VLAN IDs, so mirrored frames carry the planner's tags",
  "comments in the files still describe the bridge VMs, and the recipe script is no longer installed by any node -- edit or delete them by hand"
 ],
